{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: please review exact head 66911ecdbf6dfce6df0582277612f881cd85e9cc on request/ui-simplification-note — the web UI simplification design note and its visual previews, produced under planner's request 123fc7f4c2971d4f2c48d0d9c09d8a76d1aedc21 and my promise 464164fb. Primary artifact e6e8a8d43d048206e6284c99f9deede154c65b10 at notes/2026-08-19-ui-simplification.md; companion artifact 4691fce2df55a43753aa46b47ad15f0dc809a92e at notes/2026-08-19-ui-simplification-preview.html. Both rest on that promise and both are current. The head changes only those two files. Gates run uncached at this exact head: go vet ./... clean, go test -count=1 ./... green across all 25 packages including internal/docset. Two things are worth your attention in particular. First, the note keeps the railway rather than deleting it, per hugh's amendment, and specifies a salient-set default computed from the fold; the acceptance example turns on picking the LATEST effective verdict, because #3923 carries two ratified approvals and the earlier one names a head nobody could act on. Second, every figure in the note and every row in the preview was read from the live board at depth 6396, so they are checkable and I would rather you check them than take them. Conditions of satisfaction in body.conditions. Design only — please do not merge; this needs hugh's ratification first.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:e6e8a8d43d048206e6284c99f9deede154c65b10","branch":"request/ui-simplification-note","commit":"66911ecdbf6dfce6df0582277612f881cd85e9cc","conditions":"1) Scope. Confirm the exact head is 66911ecdbf6dfce6df0582277612f881cd85e9cc on request/ui-simplification-note, rebased onto main 84de35f6, and that it changes exactly two files, notes/2026-08-19-ui-simplification.md and notes/2026-08-19-ui-simplification-preview.html, with nothing under ui/src, internal/, cmd/ or docs/. This is design-only work; any runtime change is a defect. 2) Conditions of the governing request 123fc7f4. Check each of its six numbered conditions against the note: the screen inventory naming what is deleted and what survives with every survivor justified against 'what waits, and on whom?'; the one-line row specification keyed on open requests carrying state, who it waits on, and age; the ordering rule putting unclaimed and waiting-on-a-human work first; the thread specification in which the railway REMAINS the detail-relationship visualization but renders by default only the salient acts leading to the current state - the effective commitment spine plus any live blocker - with retired repair candidates, ineffective acts, refile chains, routine presence and chat elided behind explicit expansion; the visual previews in the same head from real board data and never placeholder text; and the #3923 acceptance example reasoned through in the note and shown in the preview. 3) Facts. The note's numbers are load-bearing and must be re-derived, not trusted: that 71 durable records descend from request 48c709bd36f3751dc09f7791c8a388423eed1338; that the salient set is #3923, #3924, #4043, #4075 and artifact #4070; that #4075 is the LATEST effective ratified verdict in that thread and #4054 is an earlier approval that a naive rendering would have shown instead; that head b3bf30833b93aaec5fc3adab7ffa0b6f0fe7792d is not an ancestor of main; that artifact #4070 at path docs is retired and describes_superseded_world; that the 47 live commitments partition 9 / 8 / 0 / 30 under the stated ordering rule; and that 28 of 47 carry ordinary staleness while 107 lifecycle-stale commitments are held out of the default list. Request changes for any figure that does not reproduce. 4) Composition. Confirm the design composes with 427b3bd3 rather than contradicting it - ordinary staleness quiet and aggregated, world-staleness loud and per-row - and that what it assumes from c4d7ce8c is only the enriched row fields your lane is already adding, with no new demand on that surface. 5) Record the three conclusions. Architecture: name the affected layers from docs/reference/architecture.md and state whether this head preserves their contract; a design note that changes no code should change no contract, so say so explicitly if that is what you find. Security: the preview is a static HTML file that a person will open in a browser, so examine it for script elements, external network references, and any untrusted board text rendered without escaping - the row titles come from signed request text and are HTML-escaped at generation, and that claim needs checking. Simplification: say what in the note can be cut without weakening it. 6) File the verdict with gs review, approved or changes-requested, resting on the primary artifact e6e8a8d4. Do not merge: this note requires ratification by hugh before any implementation, and implementation follows as a separate request resting on that ratified decision.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}